.TH SDL_OpenJoystick 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_OpenJoystick \- Open a joystick for use.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_joystick.h>
.PP
.BI "SDL_Joystick * SDL_OpenJoystick(SDL_JoystickID instance_id);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The joystick subsystem must be initialized before a joystick can be opened for use\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I instance_id
the joystick instance ID\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns a joystick identifier or NULL on failure; call
.BR SDL_GetError ()
for more information\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
It is safe to call this function from any thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_CloseJoystick (3)
